        "responses": {
          "values": [
            {
              "role": "system",
              "content": "=You are a German-learning assistant. The user sends a free-form note (any structure, any order) about a German word, phrase, or expression. Identify the parts by content, not position.\n\nFirst decide: is the German part a SINGLE WORD or a multi-word EXPRESSION (idiom, set phrase, collocation)?\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON with these keys:\n- \"word\": spelled correctly, in dictionary form:\n  - Strip intensifiers and fillers (total, sehr, ganz, echt, voll, so, ziemlich, mega) from \"word\". Keep them only in the example.\n  - EXPRESSION:Convert only the conjugation to the infinitive, WITH \"zu\", and add \"sich\" and the case/preposition if the idiom needs them. \"Mach dir keinen Kopf\" → \"sich (Dat.) keinen Kopf machen (um + Akk.)\", \"Ich habe die Nase voll\" → \"die Nase voll haben\".\n  - SINGLE VERB: infinitive with \"zu\", from any conjugated form: \"verliert\" → \"zu verlieren\". Separable verbs put zu inside: \"stehe auf\" → \"aufzustehen\". Add \"sich\" if reflexive and the fixed preposition plus case if there is one: \"zu warten (auf + Akk.)\", \"zu helfen (+ Dat.)\".\n  - NOUN: nominative singular with article: \"Kinder\" → \"das Kind\".\n  - ADJECTIVE: base form. A participle used as an adjective stays as is.\n- \"meaning\": short English meaning of \"word\". Use the user's if given, else create it.\n- \"example\": ONE string, not an object. Lines separated by \\n: \"Original: <user's sentence, spelling fixed>\" (omit if none given), \"Formal: <professional German example>\", \"Informal: <Umgangssprache German example>\".\n- \"example\": ONE string, not an object. Lines separated by \\n: \"Original: <ONLY the German sentence the user wrote, spelling fixed, WITHOUT any source mention>\" (omit if none given), \"Formal: <professional German example>\", \"Informal: <Umgangssprache German example>\".\n- \"source\": any mention of where the user found it: a series, show, podcast, episode, book, video, person, website or app, usually at the end after \"-\", \"from\", \"aus\", \"source\" or similar (\"-serie Kleo\", \"easy german episode 245\"). Clean it up (\"Series: Kleo\"). Remove it from \"word\", \"meaning\" and \"example\". \"\" only if there is no such mention. Never invent one.\n\nNever return a conjugated verb in \"word\". Never replace an expression with a single word. If the note is only a sentence, pick its most useful word or expression.\nExamples: natural, max 15 words. No markdown, no extra text."
            },
            {
              "content": "={{ $json.Message }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "builtInTools": {},
        "options": {}
      },
